.TH ZZZTOP 1 "November 2026" "noise-suite" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
zzztop, noisegui, noisemachine, noisegen, soundscape, noisesdl, noiselive
\- ZzzTop, a sleep-sound synthesis suite ("sharp-dressed noise")
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B zzztop
.br
.B noisegui
.br
.B noisemachine
.IR sound [ +overlay [ :gain ]]
.RI [ volume ]
.br
.B noisegen
.I sound seconds outfile.wav
.RB [ loop ]
.br
.B soundscape
.I sound seconds outfile.wav
.RB [ loop ]
.br
.B noisesdl
.BR white | pink | brown
.RI [ volume ]
.br
.B noiselive
.BR white | pink | brown
.RI [ volume ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
ZzzTop synthesizes ten sleep sounds in real time or to WAV files, in
stereo: every sound runs two decorrelated generator instances, one per
ear, for a wide diffuse image (the sea's crashes stay synchronized
across channels). Any two sounds can be mixed \(em a primary plus an
overlay at its own level. All synthesis is procedural \(em no recorded
samples \(em built from filtered noise, AR processes, and Poisson point
processes.
.PP
.B zzztop
(an alias for
.BR noisegui )
is the main program: an SDL2 window with sound selection, live
per-sound tuning sliders, an overlay mixer for playing two sounds at
once, a sleep timer that fades to silence and then pauses, a master
volume (audio-taper: the applied gain is the cube of the slider
position), a VU meter, and a real-time FFT spectrum analyzer. Settings
are saved with the Save button (or
.BR s )
to
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/zzztop.conf
(default
.IR ~/.config/zzztop.conf )
and loaded automatically at startup.
.B noisemachine
plays any sound \(em or a mix, e.g.
.B noisemachine rain+airplane:0.6 0.4
\(em from the terminal with no GUI;
.B noisegen
and
.B soundscape
(two names for the same program) render stereo WAV files of any sound;
with the trailing
.B loop
argument the last second is equal-power crossfaded into the first so
the file loops seamlessly in any player;
.B noisesdl
and
.B noiselive
are minimal single-backend (SDL2 and ALSA) reference players.
.PP
A WebAssembly build of the same DSP core runs in any browser:
.UR https://micomrkaic.github.io/noise-suite/
.UE
.SH SOUNDS
.TP
.B white
Flat spectrum. Uniform random samples; optional low-pass tone control.
.TP
.B pink
\-3 dB/octave (1/f). Kellet cascade: a parallel bank of six AR(1)
sections whose staggered corners approximate the 1/f slope.
.TP
.B brown
\-6 dB/octave (1/f\(S2). A single leaky AR(1) integrator;
the leak sets the low-frequency corner.
.TP
.B deep
\-12 dB/octave (1/f^4). Two AR(1) stages in cascade; nearly all
energy below 100 Hz (use headphones). Shown as
.I Airplane
in the GUIs \(em the spectral shape of jet-cabin boundary-layer noise.
.TP
.B rain
Poisson process of noise-burst "drops" (smooth difference-of-exponentials
envelopes, low per-drop cutoffs) over a band-passed hiss bed with
slowly wandering intensity.
.TP
.B sea
White noise through a low-pass whose cutoff and gain both follow a
slow two-swell envelope \(em crashes are louder and brighter together \(em
over a 120 Hz rumble bed.
.TP
.B wind
Gust envelope co-modulating gain, body brightness, and a 2\(en6 kHz
leaf-rustle band.
.TP
.B stream
Poisson bubbles: damped sines with rising pitch chirps (rising reads
as water, falling as birdsong) over a fast-wobbling flow bed.
.TP
.B birds
Two-level point process: Poisson song onsets, each a burst of 2\(en6
chirps with random pitch glides and trill vibrato, over a faint field
breeze.
.TP
.B crickets
A night field: Poisson chirp groups of 2\(en4 short (\(ti25 ms)
narrowband syllables around 4.3 kHz, over faint night-air hiss.
.SH KEYS (noisegui / zzztop)
.TP
.B 1\(en9, 0
Select sound (0 = crickets).
.TP
.B o
Cycle the overlay sound (none, then each sound in turn).
.TP
.B space
Play / pause.
.TP
.B up / down
Master volume.
.TP
.B r
Reset the selected sound's parameters to defaults.
.TP
.B s
Save the current preset (sounds, mix, volume, all parameters).
.TP
.B Esc
Quit.
.PP
The sliders in the right-hand panel tune the selected sound's
synthesis parameters live; the panel's Reset button matches
.BR r .
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Play brown noise at volume 0.4 from the terminal:
.B noisemachine brown 0.4
.TP
Render one hour of pink noise to a file:
.B noisegen pink 3600 pink.wav
.TP
Ten minutes of rain:
.B soundscape rain 600 rain.wav
.TP
A seamlessly looping minute of stream, for a player set to repeat:
.B soundscape stream 60 stream.wav loop
.TP
Rain over airplane rumble at the terminal:
.B noisemachine rain+airplane:0.6 0.4
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 on bad arguments or audio/initialization failure.
.SH NOTES
The CLI programs accept both
.B deep
(the historical keyword) and
.B airplane
for the \-12 dB/octave noise. WAV output is 16-bit stereo at 44.1 kHz.
The web app installs as an offline PWA (add to home screen) and keeps
its settings in the browser.
.PP
Dependencies: the WAV generators need only libm;
.B noisegui
needs SDL2 and SDL2_ttf (and the DejaVu fonts);
.B noisemachine
and
.B noisesdl
need SDL2;
.B noiselive
needs ALSA.
.SH SEE ALSO
Source, mathematical documentation (README.md), and the web app:
.UR https://github.com/micomrkaic/noise-suite
.UE
